        "content": "\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ruleSpecificity, survivorshipRuleSchema } from \"@/types/rules\";\n\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it(\"scores wildcard/wildcard lowest\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ id: \"1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"\" })).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it(\"scores exact field + exact entityType highest\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ id: \"1\", field: \"owner\", entityType: \"account\", strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"\" })).toBe(3);\n  });\n  it(\"field beats entityType in weighting (field=2, entityType=1)\", () => {\n    const fieldOnly = ruleSpecificity({ id: \"1\", field: \"owner\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"\" });\n    const typeOnly = ruleSpecificity({ id: \"1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"account\", strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"\" });\n    expect(fieldOnly).toBeGreaterThan(typeOnly);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema refine\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects prefer_source without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\", description: \"d\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts prefer_source with preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\", preferredSourceId: \"src_1\", description: \"d\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts non-prefer_source strategies without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    expect(survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"d\",\n    }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "6. Zod schema boundary tests — **no schema in `types/*` has a single test**",
        "content": "\nThese are the \"tool contract\" mirroring `engine/pipeline/schema.py` — a silent drift here breaks the engine/web contract with no test to catch it.\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { sourceConfigSchema, createSourceSchema } from \"@/types/source\";\nimport { severitySchema } from \"@/types/conflict\";\nimport { reviewActionSchema } from \"@/types/resolution\";\nimport { runStatsSchema } from \"@/types/run\";\n\ndescribe(\"sourceConfigSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty objects array\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"filter is optional\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [\"Account\"] }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createSourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an 81-char name (boundary above max 80)\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"a\".repeat(81), kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an empty name\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unrecognized kind\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"x\", kind: \"bigquery\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"severitySchema\", () => {\n  it.each([0, 5, 1.5, \"1\"])(\"rejects out-of-range/non-integer value %p\", (v) => {\n    expect(severitySchema.safeParse(v).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4])(\"accepts %p\", (v) => {\n    expect(severitySchema.safeParse(v).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"reviewActionSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"override requires a non-empty overrideValue\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"approve/reject ignore extraneous overrideValue-shaped payloads correctly\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"approve\" }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown action literal\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"delete\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"runStatsSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects negative counts\", () => {\n    expect(runStatsSchema.safeParse({\n      entitiesA: -1, entitiesB: 0, candidatePairs: 0, matches: 0, conflicts: 0, autoResolved: 0, escalated: 0, tokensUsed: 0,\n    }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "7. Components — **no rendering test exists for any component**",
        "content": "\n`SeverityMark` (`components/severity-mark.tsx`) is the highest-value target — AGENTS.md mandates severity is \"NEVER rendered without the word,\" which is exactly the kind of invariant a test should pin down so a future edit can't silently drop the label.\n\n```tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"@/components/severity-mark\";\n\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4] as const)(\"always renders the text label alongside the mark for severity %d\", (s) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={s} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText([\"Cosmetic\", \"Attribute\", \"Attribute\", \"Structural\"][s - 1] as string)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n`SourceTable` — untested: empty array (renders header-only table, no crash), joins `config.objects` with `\", \"`, unknown-but-schema-valid kind still renders via the `Record` lookup.\n\n```tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SourceTable } from \"@/components/sources/source-table\";\n\nconst source = (overrides = {}) => ({\n  id: crypto.randomUUID(), name: \"Prod SF\", kind: \"salesforce\" as const,\n  config: { objects: [\"Account\", \"Contact\"] }, createdAt: new Date(), ...overrides,\n});\n\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders one row per source with joined objects\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[source()]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account, Contact\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Salesforce\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n  it(\"renders just the header when sources is empty\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[]} />);\n    expect(screen.queryAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(1); // header row only\n  });\n});\n```\n\n`SourcesEmptyState`, `Button`, `Input`, `Label`, `GlassPanel`, `CanonMark` — no tests at all. At minimum, smoke-render tests plus `Button`'s `asChild`/variant/`size` prop matrix (it drives real Tailwind class output via `cn`, which is exactly where a regression would hide silently).\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "8. Integration gaps",
        "content": "\n- **`proxy.ts` route matcher** — the public/protected split (`isPublicRoute`) has zero coverage. This is the single most security-critical piece of logic in the app (\"Anything not named here requires a session\") and it's untested. `createRouteMatcher` is testable in isolation:\n  ```ts\n  import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n  import { createRouteMatcher } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n\n  const isPublicRoute = createRouteMatcher([\"/\", \"/sign-in(.*)\", \"/sign-up(.*)\"]);\n\n  describe(\"proxy.ts route matcher\", () => {\n    it.each([\"/\", \"/sign-in\", \"/sign-in/factor-one\", \"/sign-up\"])(\"treats %s as public\", (path) => {\n      expect(isPublicRoute(new Request(`http://x${path}`))).toBe(true);\n    });\n    it.each([\"/sources\", \"/sources/new\", \"/api/conflicts/1/resolution\", \"/console\"])(\"treats %s as protected\", (path) => {\n      expect(isPublicRoute(new Request(`http://x${path}`))).toBe(false);\n    });\n  });\n  ```\n- **`SourcesPage` (Server Component)** — no test for the empty-state vs. table branch, nor the `sources.length + \" configured\"` meta string, nor that \"Add source\" only appears once sources exist. This needs either an RSC-aware test setup or extracting the branch logic into a pure function for unit testing.\n- **`lib/db/index.ts` `getDb()`** — the \"missing `DATABASE_URL` throws an actionable error\" path and the \"HMR reuses the cached `globalForDb.canonDb`\" path are both explicitly called out in comments as intentional behavior but have no regression test.\n- **End-to-end auth flow**: `requireReviewer()` → `resolutions.reviewedBy` / `audit_log.actor` — there's no test proving a reviewed resolution actually gets the server-resolved label rather than anything client-supplied (the comment in `auth.ts` states this is the entire point of the module).\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Priority order",
        "content": "1. Install vitest + testing-library (unblocks everything).\n2. `proxy.ts` matcher — security-critical, currently zero coverage.\n3. Zod schemas in `types/*` — cheap, pure, and the explicit \"engine contract\" (drift here breaks cross-service compatibility silently).\n4. `lib/reviewer-label.ts`, `lib/cn.ts`, `types/rules.ts` `ruleSpecificity` — pure, trivial, no mocking needed.\n5. `lib/server/sources.ts` / `lib/server/auth.ts` — needs mocking but covers real error paths (malformed DB row, no session).\n6. Component tests, starting with `SeverityMark` (invariant-bearing) and `SourceTable`.",
        "level": 3
      }
    ],
